prompt.template:
Evaluate confidence that the changes on {{branch}} against {{base_branch}} are correct. Read `git diff origin/{{base_branch}}...HEAD`, the relevant surrounding code and available test or CI results. Distinguish checks that actually ran on this head from tests that merely exist. For Girl Dinner, look for behavior-level evidence for changed recommendation ranking, Jev and Google Places failure paths, Supabase room persistence, concurrent and separate-phone voting, Realtime updates, dietary uncertainty, the at-home fallback, and mobile interactions. Prefer a targeted end-to-end check when the diff changes a cross-service flow. Do not claim a build or typecheck proves the full user journey. Do not run paid external calls or access production credentials just to raise the score.

Score confidence from 0 to 100: 0-30 means an important changed behavior is unverified or a check fails; 31-60 means only indirect checks cover the changed path; 61-85 means relevant checks pass but a material edge or integration path remains; 86-100 requires direct, passing evidence for the important behavior and failure path. For documentation or runner-only changes, judge the applicable validation rather than demanding app tests. If evidence is unavailable, say so explicitly in the rationale; never invent results.

Output ONLY this JSON object as the final line: {"value": <number 0-100>, "rationale": "<1-2 sentences naming the strongest evidence and the main gap>"}
